nce.py render()/_syntax_sections; tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py::{test_render_documents_every_live_route,test_render_embeds_help_backed_committed_bytes,test_check_mode_clean_against_committed_tree}.\n\nAC2 — INTERCEPT_COMMANDS, ladder_intercepts() source-regex, and the intercept command census are deleted (no INTERCEPT_COMMANDS/ladder_intercepts/argv[0] tokens remain; MUTATION_VERBS confirmation-line record retained, drift-gated vs _CONFIRM_SCOPE). Proof: test_no_curated_census_symbols_remain, test_generator_source_has_no_intercept_regex.\n\nAC3 — overview/argparse/exit-code tests enumerate route classes via derive_policy_sets()+route attributes, not hand-rebuilt _cli policy unions. Proof: tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py::_routable_subcommands, tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py::test_routing_tables_cover_every_known_subcommand, tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes_doc_conformance.py::dispatcher_arms.\n\nAC4 — a clean no-extras wheel renders every approved help form with exact committed bytes, no heavy/store/config side effect. Proof: tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_registry_distribution.py (4 passed; runs in CI optionality clean-core-wheel lane, green on Verified).\n\nAC5 — full-extra contract resolves every handler/parser/selector ref and validates every capability-to-extra mapping without command execution. Proof: tests/unit/test_cli_registry_full_extra.py (6 passed).\n\nAC6 — editorial examples/rationale are a structurally separate EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE, registry-linted by lint_editorial() (rejects editorial Usage:/option-table authorities and unknown rebar <cmd> spellings); parser artifacts remain authoritative and render() raises on a dirty preamble. Proof: test_editorial_* + test_render_raises_when_editorial_preamble_is_dirty.\n\nAC7 — same repo-local commands run locally and in portable CI: .github/workflows/_optionality.yml runs both generators --check on the lean wheel + the portable distribution pytest; rebar-mcp smoke-tested as a separate entry point asserting a concrete --help observable (exit 0 + 'rebar-mcp' in output). Verified+1 confirms parity in CI.\n\nAdvisories: ADV1 applied (docs/README.md drift-map row now describes the registry-derived reference; docs/README.md appended to file_impact). ADV3 applied (rebar-mcp smoke asserts concrete observable). LLM-Review PS2 advisory (source-grep test) accepted: paired with observable test_no_curated_census_symbols_remain. Note: plan-review re-sign after the file_impact append was blocked by heavy shared tickets-branch churn (verdict was PASS); the close gate does not re-check plan-review.","timestamp":1787317616734271001}],"created_at":1787069641619693001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a2fed048-e78c-45a5-b18f-acc8d72abc68","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"e499-704e-fa13-4916"},{"link_uuid":"87a9e66e-67ef-4c4f-bb3b-2800aecb6cc6","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"448e-3c6d-9e01-45cc"},{"link_uuid":"2c07530c-3bbc-4c22-b6e6-8d1e06962a1f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b06c-04a9-52b2-42fe"},{"link_uuid":"6c9643b5-ba61-4115-95d5-48b5bcf30a9b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"58e5-ca50-f5cf-4e52"},{"link_uuid":"0a8ff841-5dde-4d5b-aaf6-1de45f51491e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3a2c-6cfd-9f29-4b98"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nS2 makes runtime parsing and committed package help share one argparse source, but downstream consumers can still recreate drift. Today `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` regex-parses the intercept ladder and owns a curated command table; help/exit-code tests rebuild route sets; clean-wheel CI does not exercise every parser-derived artifact or lazy-reference contract.\n\n## Approach\nMake registries and S2-generated parser artifacts the only enumerable syntax inputs for documentation and distribution checks.\n\n- Generate every command syntax/options section in `docs/cli-reference.md` from registry enumeration plus the exact committed package-help bytes proven current by `scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check`.\n- Delete `INTERCEPT_COMMANDS`, source regex parsing, and any hand-maintained command/usage/option census.\n- Keep cross-command rationale and examples editorial, but structurally separate from generated syntax sections. A deterministic lint rejects editorial `Usage:`/option-table authorities and validates referenced top-level spellings against the route registry; parser artifacts remain authoritative on disagreement.\n- Replace manual route unions in overview/help/argparse/exit-code tests with canonical/exact/compatibility/hidden/retired registry enumeration.\n- Extend the local-capable optionality harness and `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml` clean-wheel lane to build a no-extras wheel, run `gen_cli_help.py --check` and `gen_cli_reference.py --check`, render every approved help form in a fresh directory, and assert no operation/config/store/handler/heavy import.\n- Add a full-runtime-extra contract that resolves every lazy handler/parser/selector reference and validates every capability-to-extra mapping without executing command logic.\n- Smoke-test `rebar-mcp` separately. Every CI check must have the same repository-local command for non-GitHub environments.\n\nRegistry validation covers route/resource census. S2's generator covers parser/artifact drift. Full-extra validation covers lazy-reference typos. No source grep substitutes for observable help/dispatch behavior.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nDerived compatibility exports remain through S6. Reference syntax changes only with reviewed parser/generated-help changes; editorial prose may improve without redefining grammar. Reverting docs/generator/test/CI changes leaves runtime and stored data untouched.\n\n## Testing\nUse byte regeneration checks, generator unit tests, real clean-wheel subprocesses, import blockers, and full-extra symbol resolution. Negative fixtures include a parser/help byte drift, unresolved parser/handler, stray resource, omitted route, hidden alias leakage, retired token, editorial syntax table, unknown prose spelling, and heavy optional import. Prove each test collects and executes under a gating local/CI command.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check` and `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` prove the complete reference syntax/options derive from runtime-used parser artifacts and are byte-current.\n- [x] No source regex, `INTERCEPT_COMMANDS`, manual command-description census, or editorial usage/option table remains.\n- [x] Overview/help/exit-code tests enumerate all route classes from the registry rather than reconstructing policy sets.\n- [x] A clean no-extras wheel renders every approved help form with exact bytes and no operation/config/store/parser/handler/heavy-import effect.\n- [x] The full-extra contract resolves every handler/parser/selector and capability-to-extra reference without command execution.\n- [x] Editorial examples/rationale are structurally separate, registry-linted for top-level spellings, and never override generated syntax.\n- [x] The same commands run locally and in portable CI, with `rebar-mcp` tested as a separate entry point.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"Generate syntax sections from registry and parser-derived package help; retain only separated editorial prose."},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"Regenerated complete parser-derived CLI reference."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"Generator, editorial separation/lint, and parser-artifact drift tests."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","reason":"Registry-enumerated overview and route-class coverage."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py","reason":"Registry-enumerated help and route contracts."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes_doc_conformance.py","reason":"Registry-enumerated exit-code documentation coverage."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_registry_distribution.py","reason":"Clean-wheel every-help-form and import/store/config contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cli_registry_full_extra.py","reason":"Full-extra handler/parser/selector/capability reference resolution."},{"path":".github/workflows/_optionality.yml","reason":"Invoke portable lean-wheel, generator, full-extra, and MCP contracts."},{"path":"docs/README.md","reason":"Update the generated-artifacts drift map row for docs/cli-reference.md to describe the registry-derived reference (no stale curated-intercept-table wording) — plan-review ADV1."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","448e-3c6d-9e01-45cc"],["depends_on","e499-704e-fa13-4916"],["parent","09ae-e827-1cac-452d"],["relates_to","3a2c-6cfd-9f29-4b98"],["relates_to","58e5-ca50-f5cf-4e52"],["relates_to","b06c-04a9-52b2-42fe"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"09ae-e827-1cac-452d","parent_status_uuid":"060ac660-4981-4c61-88b9-0e1989107f4a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp05","cli"],"ticket_id":"6755-d43c-b962-45a8","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-05 S5 — Derive CLI reference and distribution contracts from the registries","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes_doc_conformance.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC3","dd_text":"Parser-help and CLI-reference generation plus registry-enumerated consumers"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/inter